    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7305f313_29cccd36",
        "filename": "chip/g/usb_spi.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 59,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000187
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-07-29T00:43:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There\u0027s two pieces to SPI passthru:\n\n1) Shared lines (MOSI/MISO/CLK).  That\u0027s what this checks/enables.\n\n2) Chip select.  This is specific to AP/EC, and is what\u0027s checked in board/cr50/usb_spi.c.",
      "parentUuid": "8237baa2_63fc6b35",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 59,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 59,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "5097274ed3e27b11a67199b00fd0360609226a39",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "65010e8a_e95da362",
        "filename": "chip/g/usb_spi.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 59,
      "author": {
        "id": 1136059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-07-31T17:44:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "usb_spi_board_enable configures the shared lines and the chip select. \n\nWith this patch if anyone aborts an AP transaction and then tries to start an EC transaction then they will still be connected to the AP flash during the EC transaction.",
      "parentUuid": "7305f313_29cccd36",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 59,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 59,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "5097274ed3e27b11a67199b00fd0360609226a39",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
